`vec-get-byval` (stdlib/vec.tur) is inline-C, and the tree-walking interpreter
does not run inline-C (the TI7 carve-out).

This fixture has no ```c fence of its OWN, so run-turi.sh's fixture_has_inline_c
does not auto-skip it: that detector greps this file and follows `(load "...")`
one level, but the inline-C here arrives through the stdlib import instead --
the same gap arc-basic's marker documents.

The fixture is also compiled-path by subject. It pins
vec-get-byval-struct-element-returns-carrier: the tyvar-ascribed carrier of a
by-value struct element must take the carrier->concrete unbox, which is a
CODEGEN decision. There is nothing for the interpreter to assert here.
